\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =-4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+8\\int t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+8(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+D) \\\\  & =-4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+8t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=8D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={[-4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+8t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(0+8(\\frac{\\pi }{2})(1)+0)-(0+0+8) \\\\  & =4\\pi -8 \\\\  & =4\\pi -8\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302522 13194139534670 true] [17592186302521 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534670 true] [17592186302521 1041 "field-1" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302521 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302522 13194139534670 true] [17592186302521 1110 #uuid "920b4380-bbfc-5f6f-8d45-af7d11b9adfb" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302522 1034 "4\\pi-8" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534670 true] [17592186302522 1111 #uuid "02c0bcc6-a786-5720-bdac-aee2e5a413fd" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302523 1017 #edb/ref 17592186302524 13194139534670 true] [17592186302523 1089 "q-50226" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302523 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534670 true] [17592186302523 1100 "$\\int (4{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302523 1113 #uuid "7e9d38a9-3f2c-5ef9-8cf7-45c3113871ec" 13194139534670 true] [17592186302523 1145 "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4{x}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\